---
number: 245
title: Jesus, My Lord, to Thee I Cry
author: J. H. Stockton
composer: J. H. Stockton
sp_category: "18"
topic: Repentance and Acceptance
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Jesus, my Lord, to Thee I cry,
Unless Thou help me I must die:
Oh, bring Thy free salvation nigh,
And take me as I am.

[chorus]
And take me as I am.
And take me as I am.
My only plea Christ died for me!
Oh, take me as I am.

[verse 2]
Helpless I am, and full of guilt,
But yet for me Thy blood was spilt,
And Thou canst make me what Thou wilt,
And take me as I am.

[chorus]
And take me as I am.
And take me as I am.
My only plea Christ died for me!
Oh, take me as I am.

[verse 3]
No preparation can I make,
My best resolves I only break,
Yet save me for Thine own name’s sake,
And take me as I am.

[chorus]
And take me as I am.
And take me as I am.
My only plea Christ died for me!
Oh, take me as I am.

[verse 4]
Behold me, Saviour, at Thy feet,
Deal with me as Thou see’st meet,
Thy work begin, Thy work complete,
And take me as I am.

[chorus]
And take me as I am.
And take me as I am.
My only plea Christ died for me!
Oh, take me as I am.
